			<div class="content" id="post-content-3735755">
									

<p>I have always been familiar with the common phrase that seems to show up often on the site, that being &quot;Does the Black Moon Howl?&quot;</p>
<p>I am aware that there are a few responses to the question and what I know so far are:</p>
<ul>
<li>&quot;Only to startle the Sun.&quot;</li>
<li>&quot;When the Foundation crumbles.&quot;</li>
<li>&quot;Only when waning&quot;</li>
</ul>
<p>Are there more responses?</p>
<p>Also, let's discuss the actual question/phrase. What is the Black Moon originally, is it intended as something in particular, and which article used the term first? Any personnel headcanons about the phrase? I would like to hear some.</p>

							</div>

								
					
