														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4233082">
									

<p>As I understand it, it doesn't have an 'appropriate' response. It exploits some sort of side effect common to most memetic infections and lasting cognitohazards. The 'appropriate' response is 'No' or 'What?' or 'I don't understand.' Someone who's infected by a memetic agent will instead reflexively make some mystically nonsensical response.<br />
There is no Black Moon, and it doesn't Howl. It's not even a method used in formal research because it doesn't always work. But out in the field, if you suspect something's messing with your partner's head and you don't have a solid enough reason to justify taking them back for evaluation, you can say it as a quick-and-dirty test.</p>

							</div>

								
					
